<title>
Brake Flexible Hose and Pipe Removal and Installation
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A4106013">Brake Flexible Hose and Pipe Components</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Brake fluid is extremely damaging to painted surfaces.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If brake fluid contacts painted surfaces, immediately wipe it off and flush the surfaces with water thoroughly.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A4106014001">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Hoist vehicle and remove wheel. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A2406001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
This operation is not necessary when removing pipes connecting to brake master cylinder.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove dirt and foreign material from fittings at both flexible hose end and pipe end.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Drain brake fluid in reservoir. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A4106003"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1 page = "1">
<ptxt>
